# ---- RSM GI (reflective shadow maps) ----

screen.indirect_lighting                    = Indirect Lighting
option.RSM_GI                            = Indirect Lighting
option.RSM_GI.comment                    = Master switch for the RSM indirect-lighting pipeline. It gates sunlight bounce GI and all of its temporal, denoising, and spatial-reuse stages. Requires shadows.
option.RSM_GI_SAMPLES                    = GI Samples
option.RSM_GI_SAMPLES.comment            = Virtual point light samples gathered per pixel each frame. Higher = less noise but slower. Quality is dominated by history length, so keep this modest.
option.RSM_GI_RADIUS                     = GI Radius
option.RSM_GI_RADIUS.comment             = Radius of the VPL sample disk around the receiver, in blocks. Larger = wider bounce spread but more light leaking through walls. Keep it modest indoors.
option.RSM_GI_INTENSITY                  = GI Intensity
option.RSM_GI_INTENSITY.comment          = Brightness multiplier for the bounce lighting.
option.RSM_GI_MIN_DISTANCE               = GI Min Distance
option.RSM_GI_MIN_DISTANCE.comment       = Clamps the 1/d^4 falloff so that virtual point lights very close to a receiver do not blow up. Raise it if you see hot spots.
option.RSM_GI_HISTORY                    = GI History Length
option.RSM_GI_HISTORY.comment            = Number of frames the temporal accumulation blends over. Longer = cleaner and nearly free, but reacts more slowly to lighting changes.

option.RSM_GI_TEMPORAL_ACCUMULATION         = Temporal Accumulation
option.RSM_GI_TEMPORAL_ACCUMULATION.comment   = Reprojects the quarter-resolution RSM GI into persistent history and blends frames to reduce sampling noise. Disable for raw per-frame GI.
option.RSM_GI_DENOISING                     = GI Denoise
option.RSM_GI_DENOISING.comment             = Runs the depth/normal-aware bilateral GI filter after temporal accumulation (or directly on raw GI when temporal accumulation is disabled).
option.RSM_GI_SPATIAL_REUSE                 = Spatial Reuse
option.RSM_GI_SPATIAL_REUSE.comment         = Uses four binary spatial-reuse kernels to perform four depth/normal/luminance-aware reuse stages in one quarter-resolution pass.
